    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        Anatomy of a Feeling: Narrating Embodied Emotions via Large Vision-<span class="search-hit mathjax">Language</span> <span class="search-hit mathjax">Models</span>
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Saim%2C+M">Mohammad Saim</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Duong%2C+P+A">Phan Anh Duong</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Luong%2C+C">Cat Luong</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Bhanderi%2C+A">Aniket Bhanderi</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Jiang%2C+T">Tianyu Jiang</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2509.19595v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        &hellip;embodiment of emotional reactions from body parts contains rich information about our affective experiences. We propose a framework that utilizes state-of-the-art large vision-<span class="search-hit mathjax">language</span>&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2509.19595v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2509.19595v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2509.19595v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        The embodiment of emotional reactions from body parts contains rich information about our affective experiences. We propose a framework that utilizes state-of-the-art large vision-<span class="search-hit mathjax">language</span> <span class="search-hit mathjax">models</span> (LVLMs) to generate Embodied LVLM Emotion Narratives (ELENA). These are well-defined, multi-layered text outputs, primarily comprising descriptions that focus on the salient body parts involved in emotional reactions. We also employ <span class="search-hit mathjax">attention</span> maps and observe that contemporary models exhibit a persistent bias towards the facial region. Despite this limitation, we observe that our employed framework can effectively recognize embodied emotions in face-masked images, outperforming baselines without any fine-tuning. ELENA opens a new trajectory for embodied emotion analysis across the modality of vision and enriches modeling in an affect-aware setting.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2509.19595v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2509.19595v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 23 September, 2025; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> September 2025.
      
    </p>
    

    

    
  </li>

  <li class="arxiv-result">
    <div class="is-marginless">
      <p class="list-title is-inline-block"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.19593">arXiv:2509.19593</a>
        <span>&nbsp;[<a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.19593">pdf</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/ps/2509.19593">ps</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/format/2509.19593">other</a>]&nbsp;</span>
